# histogram

- Label: Histogram
- Category: Copernicus (`Cop`), Houdini 22.0.368
- Inputs: 1 to 2
- Parameters: 11 (exact, read from Houdini by hython)
- Used by the height graph: no

## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/histogram.html
- Summary (EN): Builds a histogram of how a layer's pixel values are distributed across a set number of buckets. The result is a visual graph or raw bucket counts.
- Résumé (FR) : Calcule l'histogramme de répartition des valeurs d'une couche, sous forme de graphe visuel ou de comptages bruts par intervalle.

- Inputs meaning: ["source: the layer or VDB to analyze", "active: optional layer or VDB; only pixels where it is at least 0.5 contribute"]

- Key parameters: [{"name": "Mode", "meaning": "Colored Bars, Separate Bars or Graph, which sets how the histogram is drawn"}, {"name": "Buckets", "meaning": "number of intervals; more buckets give a more accurate graph"}, {"name": "Minimum / Maximum", "meaning": "value range to histogram, typically 0 and 1"}, {"name": "Outside Values", "meaning": "Discard ignores out-of-range values; Clamp counts them in the first or last bucket"}, {"name": "Scale", "meaning": "boosts bar height or intensity for legibility"}, {"name": "Channel Scope", "meaning": "toggles which of R, G, B and A are affected"}]

- Caveats: ["If the source has alpha, bars take alpha coloring and may clip.", "With Discard, channel totals can differ because clipping is applied per channel."]

